# Every text file is checked out with LF endings, whatever core.autocrlf says
# on the machine doing the checkout. Git stores LF either way; without this
# file a Windows working tree mixed the two across copies of the same file, so
# a byte comparison of a repository's shared scripts with the template's
# reported drift where no line differed (release.mjs in 27 of 31 repositories,
# 2026-10-09), and four scripts had each grown their own normalisation.
# Binary files are detected and left as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf
